# leaselogic-pro

- This is a Next.js 16 leasing calculator deployed on Vercel and protected by Supabase email/password auth.
- Keep the auth flow intact: `src/app/HomeClient.tsx` gates access and checks `public.authorized_users.is_active`.
- Keep Supabase env names exactly as:
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`
- Local development runs on port `3010`, not `3000`.
- Prefer testing locally before risky edits; for substantive changes run `npm run lint`, and also `npm run build` when auth, env, routing, or finance logic changes.
- Do not commit `.env.local` or expose secret / service-role keys.
- High-risk files: `src/app/HomeClient.tsx`, `src/lib/supabase.ts`, `src/lib/financeCalculations.ts`, Vercel env vars, Supabase URL configuration.
- When helping future sessions, use `PROJECT_MEMORY.md` and `PROJECT_HANDOVER.md` as the source of truth for project context and operations.
- Forward calculators now include a first tab named `Kampanyalı Fiyat` in both monthly and annual modes; preserve it when changing tab order or shared state.
- Campaign mode means the entered machine price already includes financing cost; do not add another interest layer on top of that price.
- Payment plans across calculator modes should stay desktop-only and remain hidden on tablet / phone layouts.
